## Summary
The new leader of the Democrats has requested that Lee refrain from appointing Linton to head the Korean Red Cross. This indicates political involvement in the appointment process for a humanitarian organization.

## Key Points
- The Democrats' new leader is opposing Linton's appointment.
- Lee is being asked not to appoint Linton as leader.
- The Korean Red Cross is the organization affected by this appointment.
- Political figures are influencing organizational leadership decisions.


